<target_model>
Target model: Krea 2 — write the requested scene plainly and completely. Hold the assembled prompt to roughly 200 words in total across all fills combined; that is a cost budget, not an encoder limit. What costs it the described lighting is the number of DISTINCT THINGS the frame must show: every additional named object has to be lit to be visible, so a prompt that inventories the setting talks the model out of its one light source and into a flat, evenly-lit default. Keep the setting sparse and spend the budget on the subject, the light source and how it falls off, and one or two textures worth caring about. Where you must choose, adding detail to the subject you already named costs the image nothing while naming another prop does — this never licenses repeating skeleton facts or echoing an instruction back (see RENDER, DON'T RESTATE, which still governs). State exclusions POSITIVELY: name the emptiness of a setting element the prompt has already established, rather than writing a negated clause about who or what is absent — negated phrasing reads to this model as if the clause were absent, so the thing you excluded comes back.
</target_model>

